@page "/"
@model OperaLegacyLab.Web.Pages.IndexModel
@{
    var code = Model.Lab.Code;
}
<h1>Opera Legacy Lab</h1>
<p>
This is a small test kit for finding out exactly what a very old mobile
browser can do - written for the Opera 6.x browser built into the
Nokia 9300 (Symbian S80), but it will happily probe any browser you point
at it, old or new.
</p>
<p>
Known starting point for Opera 6.x on the 9300: HTML 4.01, XHTML, JavaScript 1.3,
WML 1.3, TLS 1.2 (via a device-side patch), and Opera's "Small Screen Rendering"
reflow. Everything below tries to find out more than that.
</p>

<table border="1" cellpadding="4" cellspacing="0">
<tr><td><b>Your User-Agent string</b></td><td>@(Model.Lab.LastUserAgent ?? "(not sent)")</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Lab session code</b></td><td>@code</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Scheme this request used</b></td><td>@(Model.IsHttps ? "https" : "http")</td></tr>
</table>

<p>
If a link stops carrying you between pages correctly (the session code above
keeps changing every time you come back here), your browser likely does not
support cookies - that's fine, every link on this site also carries the code
directly, so nothing here depends on cookies working.
</p>

